5. What is a Web Server?
A web server is software or hardware that receives requests from clients (browsers) and sends web pages or data back to them.
Examples
•	Apache HTTP Server 
•	Nginx 
•	Microsoft Internet Information Services (IIS) 
•	LiteSpeed Web Server

6. Roles in a Web Development Project
Frontend Developer
•	Designs user interface. 
•	Creates responsive web pages. 
•	Uses HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. 
Backend Developer
•	Develops server-side logic. 
•	Connects applications with databases. 
•	Manages authentication and APIs. 
Database Administrator (DBA)
•	Creates and manages databases. 
•	Ensures data security. 
•	Performs backup and recovery. 
•	Optimizes database performance.

